# First launch:
pip install Flask-Migrate
flask db init
flask db migrate -m "Describe schema changes"
flask db upgrade

# Future changes:
flask db migrate -m "Add brand column"
flask db upgrade

# For a renamed column or removed column, review the generated migration manually
# because the system may interpret a rename as “drop old column + create new column,”
# which could lose data. A migration should explicitly rename it, for example:

op.alter_column("items", "old_name", new_column_name="new_name")

# You should back up instance/database.db before applying migrations.

# One important caveat: db.create_all() should generally be replaced or limited once migrations are set up. 
# Migrations become the authoritative way to update the schema.